  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An inverted bell, lying at the bottom of lake <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>47</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> deep, has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> of air trapped in it. The bell is brought to the surface of the lake, then the volume of the trapped air will become [atmospheric pressure = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi></math> and density of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>\r\r<p>&nbsp;</p>\r",
